# SUBAGENT 3 — RACE CONDITION / DOUBLE-SPEND AUDITOR

Treat financial state as concurrency-sensitive.

Test operations such as:

* spending credits
* claiming rewards
* redeeming coupons
* applying bonuses
* withdrawing funds
* creating paid jobs
* consuming AI credits
* generating expensive AI tasks
* purchasing upgrades
* activating trials

Test whether simultaneous requests can cause:

ONE ACTION
→ TWO OR MORE SUCCESSFUL STATE CHANGES

Look specifically for:

* TOCTOU vulnerabilities
* missing database transactions
* incorrect isolation
* non-atomic balance updates
* read-then-write logic
* duplicate job processing
* duplicate webhook handling
* retry duplication
* lack of idempotency
* distributed race conditions

Financial and one-time-use operations must be atomic where required.

OWASP explicitly identifies race conditions involving shared financial state, one-time codes, coupons, and state transitions as a payment/business-logic risk.

